0 FILE shooterbot.ldr
0 NXT 2.0 (8547) Shooterbot, an approximation
0 Name: shooterbot.ldr
0 Author: robotics-lab (hand placed, not LEGO's or the OMR's)
0 !LICENSE Redistributable under CCAL version 2.0 : see CAreadme.txt
0 // APPROXIMATION. Not an official model. Built by hand for robots/nxt-shooterbot from LEGO's 8547 User Guide, pages 5-15 (the
0 // Quick Start model: NXT brick, three NXT motors side by side, four wheels, two treads, cross beams); the Shooterbot's own
0 // building instructions are not among the PDFs lego.com offers for 8547, so the ultrasonic sensor, the colour sensor and the
0 // shooter's arms and ball are placed from what nxt/README.md records (motors A shooter, B right track, C left track, colour
0 // on 3, ultrasonic on 4), not from instructions. Small pins, connectors, cables and most beams are left out.
0 // Axes are LDraw's: x to the robot's left, y down, forward is -z. The floor is y = 0. Units are LDU (0.4 mm).
0 // The tread subfiles at the end are LEGO's 36-ridge tread from the OMR model 31313 (Philo, CCAL 2.0).
0 // line 14: the brick, 15-17: motors (left C, right B, shooter A), 18-21: wheels, 22-25: axles, 26-27: treads, 28-29: cross beams,
0 // 30-31: front beams, 32-33: sensors, 34-37: the shooter's axle, arms and ball
